# Evaluate selective context editing

Consider whether selectively reducing or replacing context could improve long sessions beyond existing compaction and rewind.

Suggestions:
- Start with concrete cases where current compaction loses useful information or retains too much.
- Explore a context projection or an explicit summarized child rather than creating a second authoritative history.
- Consider tool-call and result ordering, provider constraints, and how users understand what the model can still see.
- A comparative experiment and recommendation may be enough before designing a user-facing editing feature.

